1
00:01:49,999 --> 00:01:51,534
Damn you!

2
00:01:59,142 --> 00:02:00,176
Ryo-sama.

3
00:02:00,410 --> 00:02:02,178
Maria, get that guy!

4
00:02:02,379 --> 00:02:03,546
But you said I shouldn't use—

5
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:04,381
I'll allow it!

6
00:02:04,581 --> 00:02:05,315
Okay, Ryo-sama!

7
00:02:05,715 --> 00:02:06,816
Get out of the way, broad!

8
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:15,158
Good job, Maria!

9
00:02:15,358 --> 00:02:17,427
I'm happy I could help you.

10
00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:19,996
Ryo-sama, who is this guy?

11
00:02:20,196 --> 00:02:22,065
A wedding gift thief.

12
00:02:22,265 --> 00:02:26,336
I ran into him at the wedding of my childhood friend from Asakusa.

13
00:02:26,536 --> 00:02:29,205
So that's why you're wearing a suit now.

14
00:02:29,406 --> 00:02:30,740
You look great!

15
00:02:30,974 --> 00:02:33,243
Nah, this is too stuffy for me.

16
00:02:33,443 --> 00:02:35,745
What's with the kimono? Dressing up for something?

17
00:02:35,979 --> 00:02:37,680
I'm on my way home from a tea party.

18
00:02:37,881 --> 00:02:39,582
It suits you very well.

19
00:02:39,816 --> 00:02:41,184
I'm so happy, Ryo-sama!

20
00:02:41,384 --> 00:02:43,353
Hey, stop it in public. Huh?

21
00:02:44,154 --> 00:02:46,289
That arrest messed up your kimono.

22
00:02:46,523 --> 00:02:49,759
Oh dear, I can't go home like this. It's far too embarrassing.

23
00:02:49,993 --> 00:02:51,594
Can't you fix it yourself?

24
00:02:52,195 --> 00:02:53,396
No...

25
00:02:54,597 --> 00:02:56,166
What should I do...?

26
00:02:56,366 --> 00:02:58,601
My folks' place is just around the corner!

27
00:02:58,835 --> 00:03:00,103
I'll get my mom to fix it up.

28
00:03:00,303 --> 00:03:03,206
Really? I get to meet your mother?

29
00:03:03,406 --> 00:03:04,707
I'm so honored!

30
00:03:05,175 --> 00:03:06,209
N-No, forget it.

31
00:03:06,409 --> 00:03:09,546
Oh, come on! I'd love to meet your parents.

32
00:03:09,746 --> 00:03:13,116
What are you talking about! We're just going to fix your sash!

33
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:15,251
So, you'll take me, right?

34
00:03:15,452 --> 00:03:17,554
Nope, I changed my mind. We're not going.

35
00:03:17,754 --> 00:03:19,589
Don't be so mean!

36
00:03:19,789 --> 00:03:23,193
"TSUKUDANI SHOP YOROZUYA"

37
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:26,296
Does your family run a tsukudani shop?

38
00:03:27,864 --> 00:03:30,633
Hey, it's me! Anyone home?

39
00:03:32,101 --> 00:03:34,204
That's strange. The shop is open.

40
00:03:34,504 --> 00:03:36,639
There's money just sitting here.

41
00:03:36,873 --> 00:03:39,409
They forgot to put it away.

42
00:03:39,609 --> 00:03:42,045
What kind of business are they running? Jeez...

43
00:03:42,245 --> 00:03:44,314
It's a bit of a mess, but come on in anyway.

44
00:03:44,514 --> 00:03:45,148
O-Okay.

45
00:03:45,882 --> 00:03:47,951
Hey, Pops, Mom!

46
00:03:49,052 --> 00:03:50,820
The pot's been left on...

47
00:03:51,054 --> 00:03:53,122
Ryo-sama! There's a customer.

48
00:03:53,489 --> 00:03:55,124
Oh, it's Kan-chan!

49
00:03:55,492 --> 00:03:57,327
Hey, Auntie, long time no see.

50
00:03:57,927 --> 00:03:59,329
Oh no!

51
00:04:01,164 --> 00:04:02,365
I'll leave that to you.

52
00:04:02,599 --> 00:04:03,333
Okay.

53
00:04:05,301 --> 00:04:07,437
So, you quit your job to take over the shop?

54
00:04:07,637 --> 00:04:09,138
Not at all. Just for today.

55
00:04:09,772 --> 00:04:11,307
200 grams should be about this much?

56
00:04:11,941 --> 00:04:13,109
With a little extra.

57
00:04:13,309 --> 00:04:14,811
How generous! How much?

58
00:04:15,612 --> 00:04:18,114
Hey, there's no price tag anywhere.

59
00:04:18,314 --> 00:04:20,650
What do I do now? Ah whatever, 100 yen's fine!

60
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:21,918
Huh? Really?

61
00:04:22,118 --> 00:04:23,653
Yeah, it's a special deal today!

62
00:04:23,853 --> 00:04:26,022
It's just some shop they run for fun, anyway.

63
00:04:26,256 --> 00:04:27,690
Even if it goes under, no big deal.

64
00:04:28,157 --> 00:04:28,791
Okay, 100 yen.

65
00:04:29,325 --> 00:04:30,393
Thanks.

66
00:04:30,627 --> 00:04:34,163
Kan-chan, that woman in the kimono earlier is your future wife?

67
00:04:34,364 --> 00:04:35,532
No, no!

68
00:04:35,732 --> 00:04:37,300
Oh, come on, don't be shy.

69
00:04:37,734 --> 00:04:39,836
Hello there. Oh, it's been a while.

70
00:04:40,036 --> 00:04:41,804
Aren't you Gin-san's kid?

71
00:04:42,272 --> 00:04:44,040
Hey! Still alive, huh?

72
00:04:44,274 --> 00:04:46,276
Still got that sharp tongue, I see.

73
00:04:46,476 --> 00:04:48,578
So, you got fired as a cop and came back here?

74
00:04:49,145 --> 00:04:49,979
No, today...

75
00:04:50,179 --> 00:04:52,582
Kan-chan's getting married soon!

76
00:04:52,815 --> 00:04:54,317
What? Is that true?

77
00:04:54,517 --> 00:04:56,119
No, no, today, I just...

78
00:04:56,319 --> 00:04:59,155
Good for you! I thought you'd never get married.

79
00:04:59,355 --> 00:05:01,057
I told you, it's not like that!

80
00:05:01,524 --> 00:05:04,060
I'm done here. I'll help you.

81
00:05:04,527 --> 00:05:06,296
Whoa... She's a real beauty.

82
00:05:06,663 --> 00:05:09,299
How did you trick her? I'm totally jealous!

83
00:05:09,499 --> 00:05:11,200
I said it's not like that!

84
00:05:11,401 --> 00:05:13,069
You two look so lovey-dovey!

85
00:05:13,303 --> 00:05:14,771
Totally, totally.

86
00:05:16,139 --> 00:05:17,540
What would you like?

87
00:05:17,907 --> 00:05:20,543
Give me 300 grams of clam tsukudani.

88
00:05:20,743 --> 00:05:21,711
Sure.

89
00:05:23,179 --> 00:05:24,247
Thank you for waiting.

90
00:05:24,881 --> 00:05:26,749
Ryo-sama, how much is this?

91
00:05:26,983 --> 00:05:28,518
Everything's 100 yen today.

92
00:05:28,851 --> 00:05:30,586
Okay. Then it's 100 yen.

93
00:05:30,787 --> 00:05:33,356
Great service! You're much more generous than Gin-san.

94
00:05:33,556 --> 00:05:35,024
Totally, totally.

95
00:05:35,224 --> 00:05:37,527
If it's that cheap, I'll take this and this too.

96
00:05:38,027 --> 00:05:40,797
Oh, right, Kan-chan, when Gin-san comes back,

97
00:05:41,030 --> 00:05:45,401
tell him the senior trip is set for June 29th, okay?

98
00:05:45,602 --> 00:05:47,870
June 29th, right? Got it.

99
00:05:48,071 --> 00:05:49,639
Well then, best wishes to you two.

100
00:05:53,910 --> 00:05:56,913
Not a single win today. What an unlucky day.

101
00:05:57,113 --> 00:05:58,915
Gin-san, Gin-san!

102
00:05:59,115 --> 00:06:00,083
Huh? Yo.

103
00:06:00,283 --> 00:06:04,187
I'm glad your kid found a good wife. See you.

104
00:06:04,921 --> 00:06:06,556
What's that old woman on about?

105
00:06:10,660 --> 00:06:11,794
What's going on?

106
00:06:13,963 --> 00:06:14,597
Huh?

107
00:06:15,932 --> 00:06:17,233
Welcome.

108
00:06:22,772 --> 00:06:23,973
What would you like?

109
00:06:24,941 --> 00:06:27,977
W-Well, I guess I'll take locust tsukudani.

110
00:06:28,211 --> 00:06:29,212
Sure.

111
00:06:30,279 --> 00:06:32,281
Um, are you free tonight?

112
00:06:32,482 --> 00:06:33,216
Huh?

113
00:06:33,416 --> 00:06:37,954
If you got time, do you wanna hit up the night races at Kawasaki?

114
00:06:38,388 --> 00:06:39,922
-Ah, Pops! -Huh?

115
00:06:40,123 --> 00:06:40,757
Kankichi!

116
00:06:40,957 --> 00:06:43,226
Why are you shopping at your own shop?

117
00:06:43,426 --> 00:06:44,293
Oh...

118
00:06:44,494 --> 00:06:45,995
First time meeting her, huh?

119
00:06:46,229 --> 00:06:48,998
This is Ai Asato from our precinct. Everyone calls her Maria.

120
00:06:49,232 --> 00:06:51,000
Pleasure to meet you, sir.

121
00:06:51,234 --> 00:06:53,169
Oh, likewise.

122
00:06:53,403 --> 00:06:55,338
By the way, Kankichi, where's Mom?

123
00:06:55,538 --> 00:06:58,274
That's what I wanna know. The shop was totally empty.

124
00:06:58,775 --> 00:07:00,643
Oh, I got back late...

125
00:07:04,247 --> 00:07:05,615
I-I'm home.

126
00:07:08,651 --> 00:07:10,019
Kankichi...

127
00:07:10,253 --> 00:07:13,623
Kankichi! You actually came back!

128
00:07:13,823 --> 00:07:16,192
I'm just so happy to see you!

129
00:07:16,426 --> 00:07:18,261
C-Cut it out in public!

130
00:07:19,495 --> 00:07:21,731
Where did you go, leaving the shop?

131
00:07:22,331 --> 00:07:23,666
Just out shopping.

132
00:07:23,866 --> 00:07:27,537
Once things settle down at the shop, help Maria with her kimono fitting.

133
00:07:27,737 --> 00:07:29,505
Got it, no problem.

134
00:07:29,706 --> 00:07:31,207
Hey, thanks.

135
00:07:32,141 --> 00:07:34,444
Hey, Pa, who's that cute girl?

136
00:07:34,644 --> 00:07:36,279
She's his coworker in the precinct,

137
00:07:36,479 --> 00:07:38,448
but rumor has it she's Kankichi's girl.

138
00:07:38,648 --> 00:07:42,051
I knew it! She even came by in a kimono.

139
00:07:42,285 --> 00:07:45,288
This could be something.

140
00:07:47,757 --> 00:07:49,325
Mom, are you done yet?

141
00:07:49,525 --> 00:07:51,027
Just about finished.

142
00:07:53,162 --> 00:07:55,832
There, all set.

143
00:07:56,032 --> 00:07:57,400
Thank you so much.

144
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,868
Now, I'll ask straight,

145
00:07:59,569 --> 00:08:01,170
Maria-san, do you love Kankichi?

146
00:08:01,370 --> 00:08:02,872
Yes, of course!

147
00:08:03,372 --> 00:08:04,774
Oh my God!

148
00:08:06,309 --> 00:08:07,543
It's not a dream.

149
00:08:07,844 --> 00:08:09,879
Hey Pa, come here quick!

150
00:08:10,913 --> 00:08:12,014
What now?

151
00:08:12,215 --> 00:08:12,882
Listen, Pa...

152
00:08:13,249 --> 00:08:14,383
Whaaat!

153
00:08:14,917 --> 00:08:16,486
Is that true, Ma?

154
00:08:17,587 --> 00:08:22,058
If she loves him, then that's basically a done deal!

155
00:08:22,592 --> 00:08:25,061
He must've made up his mind to take over the shop.

156
00:08:25,628 --> 00:08:27,196
That's our eldest son.

157
00:08:27,396 --> 00:08:29,899
He's been thinking ahead all along.

158
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:33,336
Maria-san, please take good care of Kankichi.

159
00:08:33,536 --> 00:08:34,704
Please be good to him.

160
00:08:34,904 --> 00:08:37,507
O-Of course, I will.

161
00:08:37,707 --> 00:08:40,076
I hope you two get along for a long time.

162
00:08:41,344 --> 00:08:44,046
What's with all the stiff greetings?

163
00:08:44,247 --> 00:08:46,382
Maria, if you're done, let's go.

164
00:08:46,582 --> 00:08:48,885
Since we're here, I'll show you Sensoji Temple.

165
00:08:49,218 --> 00:08:51,053
Good idea. Go on, go on!

166
00:08:51,254 --> 00:08:51,888
Yes!

167
00:08:52,255 --> 00:08:52,889
See ya.

168
00:08:53,222 --> 00:08:54,457
Thank you for everything.

169
00:08:54,657 --> 00:08:55,558
Please come again.

170
00:08:55,758 --> 00:08:56,392
I will!

171
00:08:56,726 --> 00:08:57,760
Oh, I forgot.

172
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:59,662
Kankichi, when's the big day?

173
00:09:02,265 --> 00:09:04,667
...the senior trip is set for June 29th, okay?

174
00:09:05,368 --> 00:09:07,136
Oh, June 29th.

175
00:09:07,370 --> 00:09:08,070
Got it!

176
00:09:08,771 --> 00:09:10,006
Hey, it's a lucky day!

177
00:09:10,373 --> 00:09:13,009
Oh yeah? He decides when it counts.

178
00:09:13,242 --> 00:09:14,944
Ma, let's send them off with a big cheer.

179
00:09:15,144 --> 00:09:16,012
Good idea.

180
00:09:16,445 --> 00:09:19,415
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

181
00:09:19,815 --> 00:09:22,618
Cut it out! This is embarrassing! Maria, let's go.

182
00:09:22,818 --> 00:09:23,452
Okay.

183
00:09:23,786 --> 00:09:27,857
Banzai! Banzai! Banzai! Banzai!

184
00:09:28,591 --> 00:09:30,459
Pa, isn't that wonderful?

185
00:09:30,793 --> 00:09:31,561
Yeah.

186
00:09:32,628 --> 00:09:36,566
It's just the senior trip date. Why are those two idiots so excited?

187
00:09:39,302 --> 00:09:42,839
Well, what a lovely young lady. Just like Beauty and the Beast.

188
00:09:43,039 --> 00:09:46,342
Kankichi should just say they're engaged already.

189
00:09:46,976 --> 00:09:50,112
That's just his old-town spirit. He's shy about this kind of thing.

190
00:09:50,313 --> 00:09:52,448
I can tell. Yup, yup.

191
00:09:52,648 --> 00:09:55,351
Anyway, this is all just too good to be true.

192
00:09:56,118 --> 00:09:58,354
So, I guess I'm gonna have a daughter too.

193
00:09:58,988 --> 00:10:01,157
Which means, maybe even that someday...

194
00:10:01,357 --> 00:10:03,960
Here you go, Father. Say Ahh.

195
00:10:04,694 --> 00:10:05,828
Ahh.

196
00:10:07,697 --> 00:10:09,799
How is it, Father?

197
00:10:09,999 --> 00:10:12,068
Mmm, delicious!

198
00:10:13,269 --> 00:10:15,204
Even things like this...

199
00:10:15,638 --> 00:10:17,006
How's that, Father?

200
00:10:17,206 --> 00:10:19,876
Oooh, it feels so good.

201
00:10:20,076 --> 00:10:22,178
Now, how about the front, too?

202
00:10:22,378 --> 00:10:23,212
Oh no!

203
00:10:23,980 --> 00:10:26,382
And then, she starts helping with the tsukudani too.

204
00:10:29,218 --> 00:10:31,754
Father, could you have a taste?

205
00:10:42,231 --> 00:10:43,165
Terrible!

206
00:10:46,302 --> 00:10:48,704
Far from the Ryotsu family's 300-year flavor!

207
00:10:48,904 --> 00:10:49,672
Still too sweet!

208
00:10:50,106 --> 00:10:52,174
I'm so sorry, Father.

209
00:10:53,342 --> 00:10:57,079
Don't cry, Maria. The way of tsukudani is long and steep.

210
00:10:57,313 --> 00:10:59,682
But you'll master it with me, step by step.

211
00:11:00,750 --> 00:11:01,717
Father!

212
00:11:01,917 --> 00:11:04,720
There, there...

213
00:11:08,124 --> 00:11:10,426
Oh man, how embarrassing, Ma!

214
00:11:10,660 --> 00:11:12,428
Getting a daughter changes my life.

215
00:11:12,662 --> 00:11:14,930
This is just too good!

216
00:11:18,534 --> 00:11:22,338
Look at you grinning to yourself. You're creepin' me out.

217
00:11:24,106 --> 00:11:27,143
But I think she'll make a good poster girl.

218
00:11:27,610 --> 00:11:30,046
I'm sure the customers will be flooding in!

219
00:11:30,246 --> 00:11:31,280
Hello there!

220
00:11:32,081 --> 00:11:34,150
I heard your son's finally getting married.

221
00:11:34,784 --> 00:11:36,385
A gift from the neighborhood group.

222
00:11:36,786 --> 00:11:38,220
Oh, thank you kindly.

223
00:11:38,421 --> 00:11:39,989
You must be relieved, Gin-san.

224
00:11:40,222 --> 00:11:43,726
It feels like a weight's finally off my shoulders. Right, Ma?

225
00:11:43,926 --> 00:11:44,894
You said it, Pa.

226
00:11:45,161 --> 00:11:49,398
Well, our boy's finally decided to settle down.

227
00:11:49,598 --> 00:11:52,635
I can't tell you how long I've wanted for this day.

228
00:11:52,835 --> 00:11:54,370
I know, Yone-chan.

229
00:11:54,570 --> 00:11:56,172
No waaay!

230
00:11:56,405 --> 00:11:58,708
That Kankichi is finally getting married!

231
00:11:58,908 --> 00:11:59,942
Well, it seems so.

232
00:12:00,142 --> 00:12:01,777
Thinking back, it's been decades

233
00:12:01,978 --> 00:12:04,847
since he knocked over gravestones like dominoes at age five.

234
00:12:05,081 --> 00:12:07,149
That troublemaker's finally tying the knot.

235
00:12:07,383 --> 00:12:09,719
So I'd like to ask you to help plan the wedding.

236
00:12:10,286 --> 00:12:12,722
All right! I'll make sure to keep the day free.

237
00:12:13,322 --> 00:12:14,657
Thank you so much.

238
00:12:15,157 --> 00:12:17,827
For the reception, I'll offer the Phoenix Hall over there.

239
00:12:18,027 --> 00:12:18,728
What?!

240
00:12:22,832 --> 00:12:24,300
A-Amazing!

241
00:12:24,633 --> 00:12:26,569
Gin-san! Gin-san!

242
00:12:28,437 --> 00:12:29,605
What's up?

243
00:12:29,972 --> 00:12:31,440
You won't believe this.

244
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:36,011
The whole shopping district's throwing a parade for the wedding.

245
00:12:36,212 --> 00:12:37,613
Whaaat?!

246
00:12:37,947 --> 00:12:39,882
This is gonna be one heck of a celebration!

247
00:12:40,116 --> 00:12:42,518
All right, if we're doing this, we're going all out!

248
00:12:42,752 --> 00:12:44,019
Sounds good!

249
00:13:10,346 --> 00:13:11,714
That's some rough driving.

250
00:13:12,248 --> 00:13:13,783
Hey, Ryotsu!

251
00:13:13,983 --> 00:13:16,719
Why did you hide you were getting married?

252
00:13:16,986 --> 00:13:18,487
Ryotsu is getting married?!

253
00:13:18,687 --> 00:13:19,321
No way...

254
00:13:19,522 --> 00:13:20,389
Y-You're kidding!

255
00:13:20,623 --> 00:13:23,893
I got a call from your father yesterday asking me to give a speech.

256
00:13:24,093 --> 00:13:27,396
W-Wait a minute! Who the heck am I marrying?

257
00:13:27,830 --> 00:13:28,998
He didn't go into details,

258
00:13:29,198 --> 00:13:32,902
but he said a beautiful woman in a kimono came to greet him with you last week.

259
00:13:33,102 --> 00:13:35,371
I'm not going out with a beautiful woman! Huh?

260
00:13:35,738 --> 00:13:37,073
-Ah, maybe! -Maybe!

261
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:38,741
What do you mean?

262
00:13:38,941 --> 00:13:42,244
Well, I went to my parents' house with Maria the other day.

263
00:13:42,478 --> 00:13:43,679
Oh, I see.

264
00:13:44,346 --> 00:13:48,084
That's why they've been acting strange since I introduced them to Maria.

265
00:13:48,551 --> 00:13:49,852
What do you mean?!

266
00:13:50,052 --> 00:13:51,954
I can't breathe, Chief!

267
00:13:52,188 --> 00:13:53,856
Didn't you tell them Maria is a man?

268
00:13:54,056 --> 00:13:56,125
I forgot to tell them.

269
00:13:57,259 --> 00:13:59,595
I think they mistook you for his fiancée.

270
00:13:59,829 --> 00:14:01,597
So are we getting married?

271
00:14:02,198 --> 00:14:03,666
Oh, I'm so happy!

272
00:14:03,866 --> 00:14:07,369
Wait a sec! That's not possible! We're both guys.

273
00:14:07,570 --> 00:14:10,139
If you miss this chance, you'll never get married.

274
00:14:10,372 --> 00:14:11,407
Just leave me alone!

275
00:14:12,241 --> 00:14:15,311
But even the chief got a call...

276
00:14:15,544 --> 00:14:16,679
This is bad.

277
00:14:16,879 --> 00:14:18,047
Maria, come with me!

278
00:14:18,247 --> 00:14:19,215
Sure.

279
00:14:19,415 --> 00:14:21,584
Chief, I'm borrowing the patrol car!

280
00:14:21,784 --> 00:14:22,618
O-Okay.

281
00:14:24,053 --> 00:14:25,621
Asakusa! Go to Asakusa!

282
00:14:25,855 --> 00:14:27,590
Uh, this isn't a taxi...

283
00:14:28,057 --> 00:14:29,859
Just go when I say go!

284
00:14:30,059 --> 00:14:31,126
Y-Yes!

285
00:14:38,234 --> 00:14:42,304
"27 DAYS UNTIL KANKICHI'S WEDDING"

286
00:14:42,872 --> 00:14:46,308
The great-grandfather of the Ryotsu family was best friends with my father.

287
00:14:46,542 --> 00:14:50,713
In his will, he said he wanted Kankichi's wedding to be a big event.

288
00:14:50,913 --> 00:14:52,314
He was a nasty little runt,

289
00:14:52,715 --> 00:14:55,951
but I'll do my part as wedding planner and make it a big event.

290
00:14:56,152 --> 00:14:59,755
200 priests from all over the country will be gathering.

291
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:03,259
Nagauta, Shigin, Japanese dance, storytelling,

292
00:15:03,459 --> 00:15:06,729
rakugo, magic, Nankin Tamasudare, lion dance...

293
00:15:06,929 --> 00:15:09,331
There will be 28 greetings from the Ryotsu family alone.

294
00:15:09,565 --> 00:15:11,634
The ceremony will last for five hours.

295
00:15:11,934 --> 00:15:14,904
Kankichi is the eldest son. It has to be a big ceremony.

296
00:15:15,337 --> 00:15:17,806
But five hours is a bit long...

297
00:15:18,007 --> 00:15:20,209
Why not just add a ten-minute interval?

298
00:15:20,442 --> 00:15:22,111
You know, like a blockbuster movie.

299
00:15:22,311 --> 00:15:23,946
That's a nice idea.

300
00:15:24,146 --> 00:15:25,848
It'll cost a lot of money, too...

301
00:15:26,515 --> 00:15:27,783
How much will it all be?

302
00:15:28,450 --> 00:15:30,386
It's already over 10 million yen.

303
00:15:30,619 --> 00:15:31,620
What!

304
00:15:31,820 --> 00:15:33,355
Do we have that much savings?

305
00:15:33,589 --> 00:15:34,590
Of course not.

306
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:35,457
I know...

307
00:15:35,658 --> 00:15:37,860
I never thought he'd get married.

308
00:15:38,327 --> 00:15:42,031
Don't worry. The Phoenix Hall can easily hold about 1,000 people.

309
00:15:42,231 --> 00:15:43,165
Yeah.

310
00:15:43,365 --> 00:15:45,701
Let's say each guest gives 30,000 yen as a gift.

311
00:15:45,935 --> 00:15:48,237
With 1,000 guests, that's 30 million yen in total.

312
00:15:48,470 --> 00:15:51,140
We get a free wedding and make 20 million yen profit.

313
00:15:51,507 --> 00:15:53,209
I see. You're a genius!

314
00:15:53,876 --> 00:15:56,645
The more guests, the more money we make.

315
00:15:57,313 --> 00:16:00,015
Since we have the budget, let's go big with the wedding.

316
00:16:01,016 --> 00:16:03,852
How about a parade through Asakusa in a convertible?

317
00:16:04,053 --> 00:16:05,220
That's great.

318
00:16:05,721 --> 00:16:07,823
Let's throw in a samba carnival too!

319
00:16:08,023 --> 00:16:09,391
Now we're talking.

320
00:16:09,825 --> 00:16:12,061
How about a boat parade down the Sumida River?

321
00:16:12,261 --> 00:16:14,163
Yeah, that sounds awesome.

322
00:16:14,430 --> 00:16:17,199
Invite 500 geisha and throw a huge party!

323
00:16:17,399 --> 00:16:20,369
Let's make it an all-night wedding, 24 hours nonstop!

324
00:16:20,569 --> 00:16:21,203
That's great!

325
00:16:21,637 --> 00:16:22,638
It's settled then!

326
00:16:22,838 --> 00:16:24,974
Um, that's...

327
00:16:25,407 --> 00:16:27,009
What the heck?

328
00:16:27,209 --> 00:16:31,247
Damn it, they turned it into a business already!

329
00:16:31,447 --> 00:16:33,983
Turning everything into a darn festival!

330
00:16:34,183 --> 00:16:36,352
They even made signs!

331
00:16:37,019 --> 00:16:41,223
And wedding crackers and steamed buns. They're getting in on everything!

332
00:16:41,423 --> 00:16:43,525
Oh, Ryo-san, congratulations!

333
00:16:43,726 --> 00:16:45,561
So this is the bride we're talking about.

334
00:16:45,761 --> 00:16:47,930
She's gorgeous. Lucky you, lucky you!

335
00:16:48,130 --> 00:16:49,398
Shut up!

336
00:16:49,598 --> 00:16:50,933
What's wrong?

337
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:52,935
Do you know where my folks are?

338
00:16:53,569 --> 00:16:56,939
I think they're at No-way Temple's No-way Hall.

339
00:17:01,377 --> 00:17:02,745
"RYOTSU WEDDING MEETING"

340
00:17:04,113 --> 00:17:05,881
Oh, here he is!

341
00:17:06,081 --> 00:17:07,950
The man of the hour has arrived!

342
00:17:08,617 --> 00:17:10,052
Hey!

343
00:17:11,020 --> 00:17:12,554
Perfect timing. Put this on.

344
00:17:13,756 --> 00:17:14,757
And this one too.

345
00:17:19,628 --> 00:17:21,230
The size is just right.

346
00:17:21,430 --> 00:17:23,799
How about this for the groom's entrance look?

347
00:17:24,033 --> 00:17:26,602
It's a five-hour wedding, after all.

348
00:17:26,802 --> 00:17:29,338
We gotta keep it interesting, or people will get bored.

349
00:17:31,407 --> 00:17:32,975
Pops, I need to talk, now.

350
00:17:33,409 --> 00:17:34,476
Hmm? What is it?

351
00:17:35,778 --> 00:17:38,047
Oh, Maria-san's here too.

352
00:17:38,247 --> 00:17:40,182
You need to introduce her to everyone.

353
00:17:40,416 --> 00:17:42,985
Pops! When did I say I was getting married?

354
00:17:43,185 --> 00:17:44,486
Don't play dumb, you punk!

355
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:45,988
What are you talking about?

356
00:17:46,188 --> 00:17:48,590
You said the date was set for June 29th.

357
00:17:48,791 --> 00:17:50,459
June 29th?

358
00:17:50,659 --> 00:17:53,595
Oh! That's the date for the senior trip!

359
00:17:53,796 --> 00:17:54,463
What?

360
00:17:54,663 --> 00:17:56,498
You completely misunderstood!

361
00:17:56,899 --> 00:17:59,501
But you're marrying her, aren't you?

362
00:17:59,902 --> 00:18:02,504
No way! Maria is a guy!

363
00:18:05,107 --> 00:18:07,976
That's a funny joke. Don't be ridiculous...

364
00:18:08,177 --> 00:18:10,345
Then see for yourself!

365
00:18:10,546 --> 00:18:11,914
Eek!

366
00:18:12,815 --> 00:18:13,849
This is...

367
00:18:15,217 --> 00:18:16,985
No! It can't be...

368
00:18:17,186 --> 00:18:19,154
You still don't get it? Here!

369
00:18:19,755 --> 00:18:21,023
"BULGE"

370
00:18:22,091 --> 00:18:23,292
What's this?!

371
00:18:23,659 --> 00:18:26,095
I've got the same thing as you, Father.

372
00:18:34,770 --> 00:18:39,174
"MAN"

373
00:18:43,879 --> 00:18:46,115
Maybe that was too much for an old man...

374
00:18:46,315 --> 00:18:47,816
I'm sorry, Father.

375
00:18:48,016 --> 00:18:49,852
Maria, that's enough. Just go back now.

376
00:18:50,052 --> 00:18:51,053
Yes.

377
00:18:55,591 --> 00:18:57,159
Hey! What about the wedding?

378
00:18:57,359 --> 00:18:59,061
That's impossible, of course!

379
00:18:59,428 --> 00:19:02,064
But the wedding planner and venue are already decided!

380
00:19:02,264 --> 00:19:04,500
Because you jumped the gun, Pops!

381
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:07,603
We can't say it was a mistake now! What are we gonna do?

382
00:19:07,836 --> 00:19:09,138
Don't ask me!

383
00:19:09,338 --> 00:19:11,540
I don't care if she's a man! Get married!

384
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:12,708
Don't be ridiculous!

385
00:19:12,908 --> 00:19:16,245
Are you telling me to give up 30 million yen in gift money?

386
00:19:16,445 --> 00:19:17,579
Oh, crap!

387
00:19:18,580 --> 00:19:19,415
Hey, Pops!

388
00:19:19,615 --> 00:19:22,217
You were trying to make money from my wedding!

389
00:19:22,417 --> 00:19:24,386
Y-You're choking me. Let go!

390
00:19:24,887 --> 00:19:27,523
What are you doing? We're still in the middle of a meeting!

391
00:19:29,091 --> 00:19:30,626
It's nothing. I'm coming right now.

392
00:19:30,859 --> 00:19:31,727
Yeah.

393
00:19:32,027 --> 00:19:33,595
Oh, okay then...

394
00:19:36,832 --> 00:19:39,434
So, how much profit after expenses?

395
00:19:39,635 --> 00:19:40,602
You can't be serious!

396
00:19:41,103 --> 00:19:43,772
Yeah, we can't cancel now, right?

397
00:19:44,439 --> 00:19:46,542
Things have gotten too big to stop.

398
00:19:47,042 --> 00:19:50,479
Fine. Let's go through it and just collect the gift money.

399
00:19:50,712 --> 00:19:52,047
We'll split the profit, deal?

400
00:19:52,448 --> 00:19:55,050
But if they find out, we'll be in big trouble.

401
00:19:55,651 --> 00:19:58,453
Don't worry. I've got a plan.

402
00:20:01,957 --> 00:20:03,926
Yes, this is Director Mizusawa.

403
00:20:04,126 --> 00:20:05,661
Oh! The cop from the other day!

404
00:20:06,128 --> 00:20:07,629
What? A mega broadcast event?

405
00:20:08,230 --> 00:20:10,666
You can see the Asakusa Samba Carnival, Sanja Matsuri,

406
00:20:10,899 --> 00:20:13,635
and the Sumida River Fireworks Festival all at the same time!

407
00:20:13,869 --> 00:20:16,138
I'm sure it'll get 50% viewership!

408
00:20:16,338 --> 00:20:19,074
Really? Tell me more.

409
00:20:23,612 --> 00:20:26,315
Dear neighbors, this is Kankichi Ryotsu.

410
00:20:26,515 --> 00:20:28,917
I'm now heading to the wedding hall.

411
00:20:35,791 --> 00:20:39,595
Thanks to all of you, I'm finally getting married.

412
00:20:40,128 --> 00:20:42,364
Are you sure about this?

413
00:20:42,598 --> 00:20:44,933
Relax. I've got it all covered.

414
00:20:45,133 --> 00:20:48,337
Dear folks, sorry for the usual trouble.

415
00:20:48,537 --> 00:20:49,838
Kankichi Ryotsu here.

416
00:20:50,072 --> 00:20:51,840
That's our Kan-chan.

417
00:20:52,074 --> 00:20:56,111
He even roped in Sanja Matsuri, a samba carnival, and a fireworks show!

418
00:20:56,311 --> 00:20:58,680
Look! Even the TV crew's here.

419
00:21:01,450 --> 00:21:04,286
Okay, zoom in! Get a perfect shot, Waka-chan!

420
00:21:04,620 --> 00:21:07,523
The car's passing the shopping district and entering No-way Temple.

421
00:21:07,956 --> 00:21:11,660
This Phoenix Hall at No-way Temple can seat up to 1,000 guests.

422
00:21:11,860 --> 00:21:14,696
Before the ceremony, the banquet kicks off the celebration!

423
00:21:27,876 --> 00:21:31,480
Is it okay for him to make it this big of an event?

424
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,382
How does he plan to cover this up?

425
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:36,652
What the heck is going on?

426
00:21:36,852 --> 00:21:38,520
No one from the bride's side showed up.

427
00:21:38,954 --> 00:21:41,156
Ladies and gentlemen, thank you for waiting.

428
00:21:41,356 --> 00:21:43,492
The bride and groom are now entering.

429
00:21:43,692 --> 00:21:45,527
Please welcome them with warm applause.

430
00:21:48,697 --> 00:21:51,133
Looks like there's no backing out now.

431
00:21:51,333 --> 00:21:54,136
So Ryotsu finally gave in and settled for a guy, huh?

432
00:21:59,374 --> 00:22:00,909
Pa, this is great.

433
00:22:01,777 --> 00:22:03,445
I'm so happy.

434
00:22:04,212 --> 00:22:06,682
Kankichi, there's no escape now.

435
00:22:10,786 --> 00:22:12,087
Aaaah!

436
00:22:12,721 --> 00:22:16,091
Sorry, everyone. It was all a hidden camera prank!

437
00:22:16,325 --> 00:22:20,362
What a surprise! I was totally fooled too.

438
00:22:21,863 --> 00:22:24,466
You guys are too good at tricking people. I give up!

439
00:22:24,766 --> 00:22:27,536
I guess I'm not the marrying type anyway!

440
00:22:27,736 --> 00:22:30,739
But you totally had me fooled!

441
00:22:32,107 --> 00:22:35,911
So it was all fake! Haha!

442
00:22:40,482 --> 00:22:42,184
Everything was a lie?

443
00:22:42,384 --> 00:22:43,185
N-N-No way!

444
00:22:43,719 --> 00:22:45,654
What was that idiot thinking?

445
00:22:45,887 --> 00:22:47,656
There's no way this is gonna work.

446
00:22:48,023 --> 00:22:48,890
Kankichi!

447
00:22:49,091 --> 00:22:52,194
This was a good chance for all the relatives to get together.

448
00:22:52,594 --> 00:22:54,730
Don't fool the shopping district too!

449
00:22:54,930 --> 00:22:58,066
Oww! You guys made money off this too.

450
00:22:58,266 --> 00:22:59,968
Give me the copyrights, you jerks!

451
00:23:04,039 --> 00:23:05,907
You tricked us, you jerk!

452
00:23:08,210 --> 00:23:10,612
-Shame on the whole family! -Give us back our gifts!

453
00:23:15,250 --> 00:23:17,419
So the wedding was all a lie...

454
00:23:17,619 --> 00:23:19,154
S-Seems that way...

455
00:23:19,521 --> 00:23:22,658
Y-You lied to us, Kankichi! No more...

456
00:23:23,325 --> 00:23:24,292
Abbot!

457
00:23:25,627 --> 00:23:26,461
He passed out.

458
00:23:26,962 --> 00:23:28,964
Abbot! Abbot!

459
00:23:37,406 --> 00:23:39,007
Wedding gift thief! Give them back!

460
00:23:39,241 --> 00:23:41,676
No way! They're mine!

461
00:23:41,877 --> 00:23:44,179
He caught a gift thief last time...

462
00:23:44,413 --> 00:23:47,182
Leaving it to him was a mistake. Not my fault.

463
00:23:47,416 --> 00:23:48,850
Ma, let's go home!

464
00:23:49,084 --> 00:23:51,420
What an ungrateful son.

465
00:23:53,021 --> 00:23:54,790
Let's go home.

466
00:23:54,990 --> 00:23:56,658
Hey, Kankichi!

467
00:23:56,858 --> 00:24:00,962
No! I'm not giving the money back!

468
00:24:03,098 --> 00:24:08,937
RYO-SAN AND THE NEW RECRUIT
